<!--
    Noelo-Lab/kuna#1629: RH850 (V850E3v5) instructions decoded as bad
    instruction data.

    The V850 SLEIGH spec had the V850E2M instruction set only, so a function
    holding ROTL, BINS, LOOP, PUSHSP/POPSP, LDL.W/STC.W, LD.DW/ST.DW, the
    register-indirect JARL, CACHE, PREF, SNOOZE, SYNCI or a hypervisor/debug
    operation ended in halt_baddata().  Seven FPU constructors also carried
    the mnemonic of a neighbour (cvtf.dw printed as cvtf.sw), and ST.W with a
    23-bit displacement stored two bytes.

    Stage: P2 decode table (SLEIGH spec fix, no option).  The bytes are the
    output of GNU as 2.43.1 for `-mv850e3v5`, laid out as one listing block
    (0x1000) and nine small functions; CLL and the odd-register LD.DW, which
    GNU as does not accept, are written from the RH850G3MH software manual.

    #1-#44 pin one decode per new or renamed constructor, #45 the unchanged
    V850E2 system-register name, #46 that nothing is undecodable, #47-#55 the
    decompiled C.  f_pushtop reads the word PUSHSP r6-r7 leaves at sp and
    f_poplast the register POPSP r10-r11 loads first; both are r7.
-->
